you know we love to celebrate our  hospice heroes here in las vegas now so  instead of introducing you to a  volunteer today southwest medical the  sponsors of this next segment want to  educate you on what hospice care  actually is take a look so let's just  start off with defining hospice care and  what that means  sure so hospice provides comprehensive  services for people who are in a the  last stage of their life typically six  months or less  okay and is hospice the place that  you know people must go  during this  actually no that's a myth um almost all  hospice services are provided in a  patient's home and that can be really  anywhere that a patient lives so that  could be a house an apartment a nursing  home group home assisted living and i  know that a lot of people  avoid hospice care because they think  it's expensive is that also a myth tell  us more about that  um that is actually a myth hospice is  covered by medicare and medicaid  and is also typically covered by private  insurance companies  typically there is no out-of-pocket  expense for patients and hospice covers  things like visits from our staff  medications supplies durable medical  equipment  anything really related to the hospice  diagnosis  care includes visits from nurses  other people on our team social services  certain therapies virtual care  things like that that's beautiful a lot  of people don't know those things and  you know some people think hospice care  means there's no more hope or you're  giving up on life let's let's talk about  that and why that's not true either  well you know patients in hospice they  continue to have hopes and goals and  just like anybody else  as a patient's disease progresses the  hospice team really helps patients focus  and their loved ones on what their goals  are at this point and what their hopes  and what can be achieved now ultimately  hospice is really not about dying it's  about living your life to the fullest no  matter how much time you may have left  let's talk about the team and and what a  hospice team consists of  sure so the team of course includes uh  nurses and physicians it can include  social workers spiritual counselors  and bereavement support but it also  includes hospice volunteers  they're a very important part of our  team  so hospice volunteers um you know they  undergo a lot of training and background  checks and they can really just perform  provide that extra layer of support for  the patient and families they can do  such things as provide companionship  support caregivers  you know allow the caregiver maybe to  leave the house for a few hours  they can share stories and memories and  allow the the patient to you know do  some life review  um they can run errands write letters  and sometimes you know it's just  something as simple as setting by the  bedside how can people become hospice  care volunteers if you're interested in  becoming a volunteer you just need to  give us a call  and interview with one of our volunteer  coordinators um you know they can help  you through the process get you set up  for training whatever your interest is  we can find a spot for you  thank you to southwest medical for  sponsoring that segment they have  locations across southern nevada for  more information just call 702-877-5199  or visit smalv.com
 

